<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Features' }) %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main class="px-3" id="main">
  <div class="hero-box text-center">
    <h1 class="homepage-title">What <span class="highlight">TrackR</span> checks</h1>
    <p class="lead px-4">
      Paste your transcript, pick your program, and TrackR works through the requirements the
      way an academic advisor would.
    </p>

    <div class="feature-grid text-start">
      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Paste your whole transcript</h2>
        <p>
          Copy the unofficial transcript straight out of Quest. TrackR reads the terms, units and
          grades, keeps your best attempt at a repeated course, and understands CR, WD, INC and the
          rest of the transcript legend. A plain list of course codes works too.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Averages</h2>
        <p>
          Cumulative and per-term averages, unit-weighted and counting every attempt — the same
          rules Waterloo uses, including the floor that averages anything under 32% as 32%. An
          approximate 4.0 GPA is shown alongside for graduate applications.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Credits</h2>
        <p>
          Units earned, in progress and still needed against the 20.0 units a four-year honours
          degree takes, plus your non-math units and how much of your failed-unit allowance you
          have used. COOP, PD and WKRPT are excluded, as the calendar requires.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>What's left, up front</h2>
        <p>
          Every outstanding requirement in one list, so you don't have to open each section to find
          out what you still need.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>This term counts separately</h2>
        <p>
          A requirement you'll finish with the courses you're enrolled in now shows as
          <em>in progress</em> rather than met — you can see what this term buys you without being
          told you're done.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Core and elective requirements</h2>
        <p>
          Every "complete all of", "complete one of" and "complete N additional" rule in your plan,
          with the specific courses that counted toward each one.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Requirements with conditions</h2>
        <p>
          Some rules ask for more than a count — two courses with <em>different</em> subject codes,
          four courses including two at the 400-level, three courses from exactly one subject.
          TrackR picks the combination that satisfies them if one exists, and tells you which
          condition is missing when none does.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Breadth and depth</h2>
        <p>
          For BCS plans, the elective breadth categories and the 1.5-unit depth requirement,
          including prerequisite chains. A course counts toward at most one breadth category.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Communication requirement</h2>
        <p>
          The List 1 / List 2 rule, and the separate rule that applies to Actuarial Science and
          Statistics plans.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>Cross-listed courses</h2>
        <p>
          AMATH 242 and CS 371 are the same course, and so are ENGL 378 and MTHEL 300. Enter
          either code and TrackR counts it correctly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-card">
        <h2>UWFlow ratings</h2>
        <p>
          Hover or tab to any course code on your results to see how students rated it.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4">
      <a class="btn btn-get-started fw-bold" href="/">Check your progress</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
